Track 2: Recipe For Rewiring Hearts
- Story & Context: Kai, a quiet programmer usually hunched over salvaged schematics, confessed to Minjun that he used to spend his allowances on the claw machine in this very mall, always hoping for the giant plush bear, and that the failed attempts made him cynical until Sora's rewired music ignited something in him, making him feel a childlike hope again. "If I trace these lines, will your feelings light up for me?" he asked, pointing at a tangled mass of wires.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A melancholic yet hopeful portrait of a young person (Kai) surrounded by complex, glowing wiring diagrams and circuit boards, gently touching a faded photo of a plush bear from a claw machine, a single teardrop catching the soft, warm light of a soldering iron.

Track 3: The Mall's Last Supper Anthem
- Story & Context: The myth among the Arcadelight community is that on the last night the "Lost Mall" was ever officially open, before its abandonment, the power surged for one final, glorious moment, illuminating every arcade game and storefront, briefly conjuring the spirits of all the joyful meals and laughter shared there, and now their music keeps that ghost-light flickering. “We sing to the echo, the feast never done,” they chorused, a collective energy washing over the dilapidated food court.
